  "question": {
    "text": "In Young's double-slit experiment,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math> fringes are obtained on a certain segment of the screen when light of wavelength&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> is used. If the wavelength of light is changed to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>, the number of fringes observed on the same segment of the screen is given by",
